{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.0539b5a3ae","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-298","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Northam Observatory is in eastern Australia. It began operating in 2018.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 10 meters.</li><li>The Eastwick Observatory is in central Canada. It began operating in 2000.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 2 meters.</li><li>Both are observatories located on remote mountaintops.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two observatorys.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The main telescope's mirror diameter of the Northam Observatory (10 meters) is greater than that of the Eastwick Observatory (2 meters).","The Northam Observatory is in eastern Australia, and the Eastwick Observatory is in central Canada.","The Northam Observatory began operating in 2018, while the Eastwick Observatory began operating in 2000.","The Northam Observatory, which is in eastern Australia, is one of several observatories located on remote mountaintops."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.b542d08cf6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-305","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Juniper Tunnel is in central Canada. It opened in 1942.</li><li>Its length is 24 kilometers.</li><li>The Ironwood Tunnel is in western Kenya. It opened in 1989.</li><li>Its length is 3 kilometers.</li><li>Both are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two tunnels.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Juniper Tunnel opened in 1942, while the Ironwood Tunnel opened in 1989.","The Juniper Tunnel, which is in central Canada, is one of several tunnels that pass under a mountain range.","The length of the Juniper Tunnel (24 kilometers) is greater than that of the Ironwood Tunnel (3 kilometers).","The Juniper Tunnel is in central Canada, and the Ironwood Tunnel is in western Kenya."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.d8124a7a98","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-312","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Wexford Tunnel is in western Kenya. It opened in 2017.</li><li>Its length is 38 kilometers.</li><li>The Pembrook Tunnel is in northern Japan. It opened in 2018.</li><li>Its length is 25 kilometers.</li><li>Both are railway tunnels.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two tunnels.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Wexford Tunnel is in western Kenya, and the Pembrook Tunnel is in northern Japan.","The Wexford Tunnel, which is in western Kenya, is one of several railway tunnels.","The length of the Wexford Tunnel (38 kilometers) is greater than that of the Pembrook Tunnel (25 kilometers).","The Wexford Tunnel opened in 2017, while the Pembrook Tunnel opened in 2018."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.58bbae86d1","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-319","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Pembrook Bridge is in southern Brazil. It opened in 1987.</li><li>Its main span is 909 meters.</li><li>The Sable Bridge is in western Kenya. It opened in 1927.</li><li>Its main span is 463 meters.</li><li>Both are arch bridges.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two bridges.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Pembrook Bridge opened in 1987, while the Sable Bridge opened in 1927.","The Pembrook Bridge is in southern Brazil, and the Sable Bridge is in western Kenya.","The main span of the Pembrook Bridge (909 meters) is greater than that of the Sable Bridge (463 meters).","The Pembrook Bridge, which is in southern Brazil, is one of several arch bridges."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.5abe7b3fa2","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-327","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Orla National Park is in central Spain. It was established in 1919.</li><li>Its area is 4,547 square kilometers.</li><li>Alder National Park is in northern India. It was established in 1940.</li><li>Its area is 2,196 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are parks known for their old-growth forests.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two parks.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The area of Orla National Park (4,547 square kilometers) is greater than that of Alder National Park (2,196 square kilometers).","Orla National Park was established in 1919, while Alder National Park was established in 1940.","Orla National Park, which is in central Spain, is one of several parks known for their old-growth forests.","Orla National Park is in central Spain, and Alder National Park is in northern India."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.2cc672cef3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-331","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lake Halden is in northern Chile. It was first surveyed in 1924.</li><li>Its surface area is 784 square kilometers.</li><li>Lake Alder is in central Spain. It was first surveyed in 1983.</li><li>Its surface area is 234 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are reservoirs created by dams.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two lakes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The surface area of Lake Halden (784 square kilometers) is greater than that of Lake Alder (234 square kilometers).","Lake Halden was first surveyed in 1924, while Lake Alder was first surveyed in 1983.","Lake Halden, which is in northern Chile, is one of several reservoirs created by dams.","Lake Halden is in northern Chile, and Lake Alder is in central Spain."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.770746f982","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-335","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Eastwick Tunnel is in central Canada. It opened in 1978.</li><li>Its length is 43 kilometers.</li><li>The Larkspur Tunnel is in southern Norway. It opened in 2001.</li><li>Its length is 16 kilometers.</li><li>Both are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two tunnels.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Eastwick Tunnel, which is in central Canada, is one of several tunnels that pass under a mountain range.","The Eastwick Tunnel is in central Canada, and the Larkspur Tunnel is in southern Norway.","The Eastwick Tunnel opened in 1978, while the Larkspur Tunnel opened in 2001.","The length of the Eastwick Tunnel (43 kilometers) is greater than that of the Larkspur Tunnel (16 kilometers)."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.4d007da5f3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-345","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Fenwick Observatory is in western Kenya. It began operating in 1925.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 10 meters.</li><li>The Cresthill Observatory is in southern New Zealand. It began operating in 1912.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 6 meters.</li><li>Both are observatories located on remote mountaintops.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two observatorys.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Fenwick Observatory is in western Kenya, and the Cresthill Observatory is in southern New Zealand.","The main telescope's mirror diameter of the Fenwick Observatory (10 meters) is greater than that of the Cresthill Observatory (6 meters).","The Fenwick Observatory began operating in 1925, while the Cresthill Observatory began operating in 1912.","The Fenwick Observatory, which is in western Kenya, is one of several observatories located on remote mountaintops."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.0d88d96afc","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-361","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Merrow Tunnel is in southern Norway. It opened in 1902.</li><li>Its length is 55 kilometers.</li><li>The Sable Tunnel is in southern Brazil. It opened in 2006.</li><li>Its length is 43 kilometers.</li><li>Both are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two tunnels.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Merrow Tunnel is in southern Norway, and the Sable Tunnel is in southern Brazil.","The Merrow Tunnel opened in 1902, while the Sable Tunnel opened in 2006.","The length of the Merrow Tunnel (55 kilometers) is greater than that of the Sable Tunnel (43 kilometers).","The Merrow Tunnel, which is in southern Norway, is one of several tunnels that pass under a mountain range."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.50f7bd285d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-362","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lake Glenrock is in southern Norway. It was first surveyed in 1916.</li><li>Its surface area is 848 square kilometers.</li><li>Lake Cresthill is in northern Japan. It was first surveyed in 2011.</li><li>Its surface area is 97 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are freshwater lakes formed by glaciers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two lakes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Lake Glenrock was first surveyed in 1916, while Lake Cresthill was first surveyed in 2011.","Lake Glenrock is in southern Norway, and Lake Cresthill is in northern Japan.","The surface area of Lake Glenrock (848 square kilometers) is greater than that of Lake Cresthill (97 square kilometers).","Lake Glenrock, which is in southern Norway, is one of several freshwater lakes formed by glaciers."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.28da9e02a4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-386","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Pembrook Bridge is in western Kenya. It opened in 1894.</li><li>Its main span is 2,037 meters.</li><li>The Glenrock Bridge is in northern India. It opened in 1961.</li><li>Its main span is 1,342 meters.</li><li>Both are cable-stayed bridges.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two bridges.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Pembrook Bridge is in western Kenya, and the Glenrock Bridge is in northern India.","The Pembrook Bridge, which is in western Kenya, is one of several cable-stayed bridges.","The main span of the Pembrook Bridge (2,037 meters) is greater than that of the Glenrock Bridge (1,342 meters).","The Pembrook Bridge opened in 1894, while the Glenrock Bridge opened in 1961."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.a8eff88de6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-395","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Juniper National Park is in southern Norway. It was established in 1995.</li><li>Its area is 2,697 square kilometers.</li><li>Halden National Park is in southern New Zealand. It was established in 1951.</li><li>Its area is 1,211 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are parks known for their old-growth forests.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two parks.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Juniper National Park, which is in southern Norway, is one of several parks known for their old-growth forests.","Juniper National Park is in southern Norway, and Halden National Park is in southern New Zealand.","Juniper National Park was established in 1995, while Halden National Park was established in 1951.","The area of Juniper National Park (2,697 square kilometers) is greater than that of Halden National Park (1,211 square kilometers)."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.847b2e5737","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-6","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Halvorsen is an ecologist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.</li><li>Halvorsen compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.</li><li>Halvorsen found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Halvorsen compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.","Because robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier, Halvorsen concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.","Halvorsen concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.","Halvorsen found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.f69f9e2f94","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-14","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Novak is a psychologist.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.</li><li>Novak had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.</li><li>Novak found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.</li><li>Novak concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Novak found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.","Because students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly, Novak concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.","To investigate the question, Novak had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.","Novak concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.59527e85b6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-22","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Takeda is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Takeda grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Takeda found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Takeda concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Takeda grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.","Takeda found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.","Takeda concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","Because fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer, Takeda concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.83cd355982","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-28","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Okafor is a materials scientist.</li><li>Okafor wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Okafor coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Okafor found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Okafor concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Okafor concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","Because coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer, Okafor concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","To investigate the question, Okafor coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.","Okafor found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.6c609d3f80","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-30","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Yara Nakamura is an entomologist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Nakamura set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Nakamura found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because bees visited the blue feeders most often, Nakamura concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","To investigate the question, Nakamura set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.","Nakamura concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","Nakamura found that bees visited the blue feeders most often."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.5ea0acd9d3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-39","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Kowalski is a sociologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Kowalski surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Kowalski found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Kowalski found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.","To investigate the question, Kowalski surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.","Because residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened, Kowalski concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","Kowalski concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.f7457faa5d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-48","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Varga is a nutrition researcher.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch.</li><li>Varga asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.</li><li>Varga found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.</li><li>Varga concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Varga asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.","Varga found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.","Because lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days, Varga concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.","Varga concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.386f4d3cac","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-53","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Kowalski is a nutrition researcher.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch.</li><li>Kowalski asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.</li><li>Kowalski found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Kowalski asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.","Kowalski found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.","Kowalski concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.","Because lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days, Kowalski concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.cb5842ac60","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-59","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Haddad is a zoologist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.</li><li>Haddad gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.</li><li>Haddad found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.</li><li>Haddad concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Haddad gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.","Haddad concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.","Haddad found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.","Because elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day, Haddad concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.be33a7b835","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-62","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Beatriz Halvorsen is an astronomer.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.</li><li>Halvorsen measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.</li><li>Halvorsen found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Halvorsen found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.","Halvorsen concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.","To investigate the question, Halvorsen measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.","Because the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days, Halvorsen concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.b8ffa890ca","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-82","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Anika Brennan is a botanist.</li><li>Brennan wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Brennan grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Brennan found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Brennan concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Brennan grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.","Because plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates, Brennan concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","Brennan found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","Brennan concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.5ef03d2f76","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-116","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Ferreira is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Ferreira asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Ferreira found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Ferreira asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.","Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","Because tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep, Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","Ferreira found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.c66e77eaeb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-124","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Quintero is an ornithologist.</li><li>Quintero wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Quintero measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Quintero found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Quintero concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings, Quintero concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","To investigate the question, Quintero measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Quintero found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.","Quintero concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.9dd64bc80b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-131","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Samuel Novak is a public health researcher.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year, Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.","To investigate the question, Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.8bd9b26d1d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-135","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Viktor Solberg is an archaeologist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages.</li><li>Solberg analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.</li><li>Solberg found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.</li><li>Solberg concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because many pots were made from clay found only far inland, Solberg concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.","Solberg concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.","Solberg found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.","To investigate the question, Solberg analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.eb0311dc37","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-150","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Chen Varga is a climate scientist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Varga compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Varga found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Varga concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Varga compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.","Varga found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","Varga concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","Because homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler, Varga concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.98ed7df0c6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-154","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Mensah is a climate scientist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Mensah compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Mensah found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Mensah concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mensah found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","Because homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler, Mensah concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","To investigate the question, Mensah compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.","Mensah concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.09a857d9b7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-171","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Varga is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Varga added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Varga found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Varga concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Varga found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.","Varga concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","Because the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks, Varga concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","To investigate the question, Varga added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.98bd527f1f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-174","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Okafor is a music researcher.</li><li>Okafor wanted to find out whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.</li><li>Okafor tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.</li><li>Okafor found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.</li><li>Okafor concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Okafor found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.","Okafor concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.","To investigate the question, Okafor tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.","Because children who took lessons improved more than those who did not, Okafor concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.b0088c4c09","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-176","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Lindqvist is a music researcher.</li><li>Lindqvist wanted to find out whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.</li><li>Lindqvist tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.</li><li>Lindqvist found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.</li><li>Lindqvist concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Lindqvist found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.","To investigate the question, Lindqvist tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.","Because children who took lessons improved more than those who did not, Lindqvist concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.","Lindqvist concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.c19a60d4ab","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-177","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Vance is a music researcher.</li><li>Vance wanted to find out whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.</li><li>Vance tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.</li><li>Vance found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.</li><li>Vance concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Vance concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.","Because children who took lessons improved more than those who did not, Vance concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.","Vance found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.","To investigate the question, Vance tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."}
